<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Developer Business Lab collects, uses, and protects information when you use this website or purchase our digital products."
  eyebrow="Legal"
>
  <p><strong>Last updated: August 30, 2026</strong></p>

  <p>Developer Business Lab respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains what information may be collected when you visit this website, request or download free resources, purchase a digital product, contact us, or otherwise interact with Developer Business Lab, and how that information may be used.</p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We may receive information that you provide voluntarily, including your name, email address, order information, messages you send to us, and information you provide when requesting a free resource or joining an email list.</p>
  <p>When you use the website, certain technical and usage information may also be generated automatically. This can include information such as your IP address, approximate geographic location, browser and device information, referring page, pages viewed, interactions with the website, session information, and timestamps.</p>

  <h2>Purchases and payment information</h2>
  <p>Developer Business Lab sells digital products using third-party commerce and payment services, including Lemon Squeezy. Checkout, payment processing, receipts, tax handling where applicable, and product delivery may be performed by those providers.</p>
  <p>Developer Business Lab does not need to receive or store your complete payment-card number in order to fulfill a purchase. Information you provide during checkout is also subject to the privacy practices of the applicable commerce and payment providers.</p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <p>We may use information we receive to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>provide products, downloads, and resources you request;</li>
    <li>process and support purchases;</li>
    <li>respond to questions, support requests, and refund requests;</li>
    <li>send transactional messages related to your purchases or requests;</li>
    <li>send marketing or educational email when you have subscribed or otherwise permitted us to do so;</li>
    <li>operate, secure, troubleshoot, and improve the website;</li>
    <li>measure website traffic, usage, and the effectiveness of our content and marketing;</li>
    <li>understand how visitors move through and interact with the website; and</li>
    <li>comply with legal, tax, accounting, fraud-prevention, and other legitimate business obligations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Email communications</h2>
  <p>If you subscribe to Developer Business Lab email communications, we may send you educational content, product information, announcements, and promotional messages. Marketing emails will provide a way to unsubscribe. Unsubscribing from marketing does not prevent us from sending transactional or service messages that are necessary to fulfill a purchase, respond to a request, or administer an existing customer relationship.</p>

  <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
  <p>Developer Business Lab uses Google Analytics to help us understand how visitors find and use the website. Google Analytics may collect information such as the number of visitors and sessions, pages viewed, interactions with the website, approximate geographic information, and browser and device information.</p>
  <p>Google Analytics may use first-party cookies, including cookies such as <code>_ga</code>, to distinguish users and sessions. Information generated through Google Analytics is processed by Google to provide measurement and reporting services to us. Google Analytics is not intended to receive information that directly identifies you, such as your name or email address, through our analytics implementation.</p>
  <p>Where required by applicable law, analytics storage and related technologies will be subject to the visitor's consent choices. Visitors can also control or delete cookies through their browser settings, although doing so may affect measurement or certain website functions.</p>

  <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>The website and the third-party services that support it may use cookies, logs, or similar technologies for analytics, security, checkout, fraud prevention, session management, performance, and other necessary functions. The specific cookies used can change as our providers and configuration change.</p>
  <p>If Developer Business Lab later introduces advertising, remarketing, or other tracking technologies that materially expand how visitor information is used, this policy will be updated and additional consent controls will be implemented where required.</p>

  <h2>Service providers</h2>
  <p>We may share information with service providers when reasonably necessary to operate Developer Business Lab. These may include Google for website analytics, website hosting and infrastructure providers, commerce and payment processors, email providers, file-delivery services, security or fraud-prevention services, and other vendors that perform services on our behalf.</p>
  <p>These providers may process information according to their own privacy policies and contractual obligations. We do not sell your personal information to third parties for money.</p>

  <h2>Legal and safety disclosures</h2>
  <p>We may disclose information when reasonably necessary to comply with applicable law, legal process, or a valid governmental request; to investigate fraud, abuse, or security problems; to enforce our terms; or to protect the rights, property, or safety of Developer Business Lab, our customers, or others.</p>

  <h2>Data retention</h2>
  <p>We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary for the purpose for which it was collected and for legitimate business, accounting, tax, security, dispute-resolution, and legal requirements. Different categories of information may be retained for different periods. Analytics information is also subject to the data-retention settings configured for our Google Analytics property and Google's applicable policies.</p>

  <h2>Data security</h2>
  <p>We use reasonable administrative and technical measures intended to protect information handled through Developer Business Lab. No website, transmission method, or storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure, so absolute security cannot be promised.</p>

  <h2>Your privacy choices and requests</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live, applicable law may give you rights concerning your personal information, which can include rights to request access, correction, deletion, or information about how your data is used. You may contact Developer Business Lab to make a privacy request. We may need to verify your identity before fulfilling certain requests, and some information may need to be retained where permitted or required by law.</p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>Developer Business Lab is intended for adults and business users and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly seek to collect personal information from children under 13.</p>

  <h2>Third-party websites</h2>
  <p>The website may link to third-party websites and services. Developer Business Lab does not control the privacy practices of those third parties. Their handling of information is governed by their own policies.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy as Developer Business Lab, its website, analytics configuration, or its service providers change. The current version will be posted on this page with an updated revision date when appropriate.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions or requests concerning this Privacy Policy or personal information handled by Developer Business Lab may be submitted through the contact methods provided on this website or in communications associated with your purchase.</p>
</ProseLayout>
